{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"For an Irish UCITS ETF, these are distinct requirements:\n\n- **Transparency-policy disclosures:** The prospectus must explain the transparency policy for the portfolio and where investors can obtain portfolio information. This describes the policy; it is not a substitute for publishing holdings.\n- **Daily public holdings:** The default is to disclose the ETF’s portfolio holdings to the public at least daily, for example on the ETF’s website.\n- **Conditional periodic-holdings route:** The 2026 regulations allow less-frequent public holdings disclosure only if the specified conditions are met. The ETF must still provide daily portfolio information to authorised participants and market makers to support arbitrage, under appropriate confidentiality and access arrangements. This restricted daily information is not the same as daily public disclosure.\n\nCBI Q&A 1012 (April 2025) should be read alongside the regulations: it clarifies the applicable disclosure expectations, but does not collapse the public-disclosure and AP/market-maker information routes into one."}}
